  "id": "isomorphism",
  "term": "isomorphism",
  "definition": "Isomorphism is the idea that similar patterns of organization and governing rules can appear across different levels of a system, such as the mind, brain, and social relationships. In this framework, it means these levels function according to comparable principles, especially in balancing stability with the ability to adapt and change.",
